# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: the HEIF plug-in, from LumenHEIF-<ver>.zip.
Package: LumenHEIF
Section: Graphics
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: Lumen (>= 0.0.37), SharedUnixLibrary (>= 1.16), ARMEABISupport
Description: HEIF and AVIF photos for Lumen (libheif)
 Lets Lumen import, show, adjust and export HEIF/HEIC photos, as phones
 take them, and AVIF photos, with libheif 1.23.7, FFmpeg 5.1.10's HEVC
 decoder (cut down to that alone) and dav1d 1.5.4 for AV1: the photo's
 own thumbnail when it has one, Display P3 photos converted to sRGB, and
 their EXIF. It uses NEON where the computer has it (Pi 2 onwards). It needs about 100 MB of memory to
 decode a 12 megapixel photo (more for bigger ones). It goes into Lumen's
 Plugins directory; Lumen finds it the next time it starts.
Build-Map: !Lumen/Plugins/HEIF -> Apps/Graphics/!Lumen/Plugins/HEIF
Build-Notice: The HEIF plug-in for Lumen, packaged for PackMan from its
 release zip.
